  "description": "EXPLORATORY (bean t7qv): tests whether the positive-sector operator selection is structural in q or an accident at q_0, rebuilding the Gram, the Markov cost TR_M(q) and both nucleon NFs at each q (gram_matrix_mp's q override exists for exactly this). Swept q = 1.02 .. 1.50 at A=3. RESULTS: (1) the T vs He3 separation holds at EVERY q tested — fully robust, and it is the claim Gap #2 needs; (2) the optimal sub-alphabet {sigma_1, L+, L-} is stable on q in [1.02, 1.26], breaking at 1.28 when gamma, sigma_0 and e- enter, with q_0 = 1.10998 well inside; (3) the degeneracy-breaking obj > u_1 holds to about q = 1.30 and fails by 1.35, where the optimum falls back onto the row-1 bound. NOT robust: the support SIZE, which drifts 8/11 -> 6/9 -> 6/7 -> 5/5 with no monotone pattern, so '6 and 9' are vertex counts and must not be quoted as invariants. Also records the owner's ruling that x_free's negative coordinates are fine: it is the FREE constituent product, and constituents are not required to be in a stable configuration. No fit; no B_AME; nothing wired.",
